        "subject": "Drop the disableViolationMonitoring config option",
        "body": "Monitoring already has exactly one switch — the enableLogMonitor\ninitialize() argument, shared with the macOS monitor — and embedders\nthat want it user-controllable can map their own setting onto it. A\nsecond, opposite-polarity option for the same feature was redundant.\nNever released, so removing it changes nothing for consumers.",
